2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“HDB” means the Housing and Development Board established under the Housing and Development Act (Cap. 129);
“refuse, waste or other article” means refuse, waste or other article collected from a residential or commercial property in the housing estates of the HDB within the Town managed by a Town Council;
“specified conservancy and service contractor” means a contractor engaged by a Town Council to provide services to the Town Council in, or in connection with, the collection of refuse from, or the cleaning of, the common property of residential and commercial property in the housing estates of the HDB within the Town of the Town Council;
“Town” and “Town Council” have the same meanings, respectively, as in the Town Councils Act (Cap. 329A).
